Subject: [PATCH] A3a: Lemma 7.10 packing, 296 of 455 roots kernel-checked

Adds the Challenge/Solution pair Packing (core Lean): a generic greedy
packing lemma, the largest-coordinate bound, the check that omega(1,1)
of Proposition 7.8 equals Table 3's omega, the root ledger (296 settled
+ 159 open = 455), and Lemma 7.10 for every settled root, over every
rough profile in Definition 7.4's domain. The settled condition-(D) root
is proved uniformly over its full (gamma, omega0) box.

Certificates (bin selections) are stored in
specs/certificates/packing_a3a.json with their generator and a script
that checks the Lean tables match; the kernel re-checks every inequality.

